Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.34 phase 2: equip in Status > Equipment without the long round trip

P6.34 phase 2 (docs/P6.34_MENU_FLOW.md, owner question 6, orchestrator default
pending confirmation). In the equipment panel's item list
(STSTATUS_chooseEquipItem, equip_panel.c), Cross on an item calls STSTATUS_equip
as before and then goes to substate 0x14, which fades the list, the slot's item
and (from substate 0) the title and the slots back in: four 10-frame panel
fades each way. With the key items_equip_stays on (default 1;
DW3_ITEMS_EQUIP_STAYS=0 or the file key 0 gives the original flow) the four
PanelAnim durations are set to 1 frame until the panel is back on the slot list
(STSTATUS_chooseEquipSlot, which restores 10 and logs the landing), so the same
state machine runs without the visible fades. panel->slot is not touched: the
slot cursor stays on the slot just changed. Triangle (cancel) is unchanged.

When the list opens (STSTATUS_closeEquipSlots, STSTATUS_enterEquipList) it
starts on the row of the item worn in that slot if a spare copy of it is in the
list (a worn item only appears in the list while a copy is in the bag), with
the cursor, the preview of the stats and the scroll bar (the USA bar follows
the chosen item, the European one the page) for that row; otherwise on "none"
as before. STSTATUS_equip is still the only writer of the equipment.

Logs (port/items_menu): "dw3-items-menu: equip-stays begin|list-open ..." and
"equip-stays slot=.. after=equip frames=..".

--- a/src/menus/field_menu/equip_panel.c
+++ b/src/menus/field_menu/equip_panel.c
@@ -4,6 +4,21 @@
 #include "menus/field_menu.h"
 #if PORT_HOST
 #include "port_items_menu.h"
+
+/* P6.34 phase 2 (patch 0190): after an equip the panel returns to the slot list
+   with one-frame fades (the original fades four panels out and in, ~70 frames).
+   The panel is a single task, so its state is kept here. */
+static s32 portQuickReturn;    /* 1 from the equip until the slot list is back */
+static s32 portQuickFrames;    /* frames spent in the quick return */
+static s32 portOpenRow;        /* the row the next list opens on */
+
+static void portSetFadeFrames(EquipPanel *panel, s32 frames) {
+    s32 i;
+
+    for (i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
+        panel->panels[i].duration = frames;
+    }
+}
 #endif
 
